  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Build one URP Lit material from a raw texture set: the photo's colour, its normal, occlusion and roughness maps. Fix how the maps are imported, set the material to the surface's real size, and use it in this corner. Keep it in your library.\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Import: pick a set in Raw-Sets. Set its normal map's Texture Type to Normal map, and turn sRGB (Color Texture) off on its occlusion map.\n2. Build: create a URP Lit material in your own folder with the Base Map, Normal Map and Occlusion Map. Set Smoothness by eye: Lit uses smoothness, the opposite of roughness. Set Tiling to the surface's size \xF7 the texture's real size (concrete panels about 2.4 m, stone paving about 2 m).\n3. Place: apply it to the wall or the floor, and compare it with Textured materials. Or start from your own photo of a surface in Milan.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Textured materials (real surfaces) \xB7 Material chart (values)</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
